1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,126
The last software in the loop lessons connect Isaac Sim's cameras to Isaac ROS,

2
00:00:06,126 --> 00:00:10,897
NVIDIA's GPU accelerated ROS packages, here for image segmentation.

3
00:00:11,797 --> 00:00:18,248
The Hawk camera on Nova Carter publishes images on the r g b topic through a ROS 2 camera graph.

4
00:00:18,248 --> 00:00:21,676
An Isaac ROS segmentation container processes them,

5
00:00:21,676 --> 00:00:27,522
and you can view the result or let your own node react and send velocity commands back.

6
00:00:28,422 --> 00:00:32,204
Only the Isaac Sim side changes in six point one.

7
00:00:32,204 --> 00:00:36,680
Start from the Nova Carter scene of lesson four point one.

8
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:40,307
Open Tools, Robotics, ROS 2 OmniGraphs, Camera.

9
00:00:40,307 --> 00:00:43,934
Pick the front Hawk left camera and tick R G B.

10
00:00:43,934 --> 00:00:50,339
Press play and check the rate of the r g b topic, or view it with r q t image view.

11
00:00:51,239 --> 00:00:58,852
One thing to watch: Isaac ROS containers often use ROS 2 Humble, while Isaac Sim publishes with Jazzy.

12
00:00:58,852 --> 00:01:05,495
Standard messages usually still flow if both sides use the same middleware and domain id.

13
00:01:05,495 --> 00:01:10,122
If they do not, start Isaac Sim with ROS distro set to humble.

14
00:01:10,122 --> 00:01:12,137
Six point one bundles both.

